      "source": [
        "### Implementing Train/Test Split for GCN\n",
        "\n",
        "To ensure proper validation of the GCN model, we will split the dataset into training and testing subsets. For graph-based learning, this typically involves creating masks that indicate which nodes belong to the training set and which belong to the testing set. This approach ensures that the graph structure remains intact for message passing, but the model is only trained and evaluated on distinct subsets of nodes.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will use a stratified split to maintain the class distribution of our risk labels across both sets, which is crucial for balanced evaluation, especially with a relatively small number of nodes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "4f2b5cd7",
        "outputId": "9e7e593f-b916-40bd-e4c4-658d211cdfb1"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Number of training nodes: 28\n",
            "Number of testing nodes: 12\n",
            "Training label distribution:\n",
            "tensor([ 9,  9, 10])\n",
            "Testing label distribution:\n",
            "tensor([4, 4, 4])\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert torch tensor y to numpy for sklearn's train_test_split\n",
        "y_numpy = data.y.cpu().numpy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Get indices for training and testing sets\n",
        "# Using a 70/30 split, stratified by risk label\n",
        "train_indices, test_indices = train_test_split(\n",
        "    np.arange(data.num_nodes),\n",
        "    test_size=0.3,\n",
        "    random_state=42, # Ensure reproducibility\n",
        "    stratify=y_numpy # Maintain class distribution across splits\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create boolean masks\n",
        "train_mask = torch.zeros(data.num_nodes, dtype=torch.bool)\n",
        "train_mask[train_indices] = True\n",
        "\n",
        "test_mask = torch.zeros(data.num_nodes, dtype=torch.bool)\n",
        "test_mask[test_indices] = True\n",
        "\n",
        "# Assign masks to the data object\n",
        "data.train_mask = train_mask\n",
        "data.test_mask = test_mask\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Number of training nodes: {data.train_mask.sum().item()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Number of testing nodes: {data.test_mask.sum().item()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Training label distribution:\\n{data.y[data.train_mask].bincount()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Testing label distribution:\\n{data.y[data.test_mask].bincount()}\")"
      ]
    },
