        "The degree distribution plot above shows how many nodes have a certain number of connections. In a scale-free network, this plot would typically show a long tail, indicating a few nodes with very high degrees and many nodes with low degrees. This is often better visualized on a log-log plot to check for a linear relationship (power-law).\n",
