        "# Part B: rectified methodology\n",
        "1. Chronological windows: features from the first 150 days, target from the remaining 71 days.\n",
        "2. Observed target: delivery shortfall rate in the target window, cut into tertiles by rank, for products with at least MIN_FUTURE_SALES of demand there.\n",
        "3. One row per product: POP001L12P.1 is merged into POP001L12P, so rows match the 40 graph nodes in the same order.\n",
        "4. Baselines: majority class, persistence, Random Forest and MLP with graph degree; GCN with permuted-node and single-relation controls.\n",
        "5. Evaluation: 5-fold x 10-repeat stratified cross-validation, scaler fitted on training nodes only, Wilcoxon tests on repeat means."
